{"name":"Red Salsa","hex":"#fd3a4a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"salsa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spicy tomato sauce of Mexican origin, often including onions and hot peppers.","A style of urban music originally from New York heavily influenced by Cuban dance music, jazz and rock."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dance the salsa."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salsa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salsa (food)","blocks":[{"text":"A salsa is any of a variety of sauces used as condiments for tacos and other Mexican and Mexican-American foods, and as dips for tortilla chips. They may be raw or cooked, and are generally served at room temperature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Various_salsas.jpg/330px-Various_salsas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salsa_(food)","wikidata":"Q249114"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg/500px-MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg/1280px-MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg/500px-MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Salsa made with jalapeños, mango, pineapple, red onion and cilantro (coriander)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMangoPineappleSalsa.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg/500px-AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg/1280px-AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg/500px-AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Various types of Mexican salsas, including moles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAGV_4558_(21982977281).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Chorizo_and_egg_burrito_with_salsa.jpg/500px-Chorizo_and_egg_burrito_with_salsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut